as the convoy arrives the trauma of the  last few months is clear on their faces  so too is the sense of absolute relief  it's taken days to make this journey but  they are now safe at this un reception  center  oksana arrived with her two children  after spending weeks underground  she tells me she thought they'd never  get out alive  the evacuation mission started on friday  through the ruins of the as of style  steel works they moved with great  difficulty  hoping the fragile ceasefire would hold  before reaching the waiting buses  evacuees were then taken to this camp in  russian-occupied territory  where they were processed  many of the families of those people  trapped inside the azerb style steel  works thought they would never see the  day when they reached this point  but there are fears for those still  stuck inside as more stories of  atrocities emerge from a city that has  been destroyed beyond recognition  others who were stuck in mario pool  managed to leave on their own taking  advantage of the ceasefire  many of them arriving in battered cars  with stories of terror and survival  inside the aid tent we meet marina  she still can't believe she's here with  her children  on her phone she shows me pictures she  smuggled out on an sd card through many  russian checkpoints  this is the center of mario paul  neighborhood after neighborhoods been  wrecked and newly dug cemeteries she  says are all over the city  there are still many civilians trapped  inside the as of star works and a large  number of fighters who are refusing to  surrender what happens to them nobody  knows  [Music]  but russia has resumed its attack on the  plants making it impossible at the  moment to get more people to safety  for those that have made it out it is a  time to be reunited with loved ones  but the memories of what they have seen  and left behind  will be difficult to forget  alex rossi sky news zaparisia
 

